course: dictionary
lesson: 11136
title: Widen: wider and bigger
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To widen something means to make it wider. It can also mean to become wider on its own. «The river widens near the sea» tells you the river gets wider as it gets close to the sea.
explain: Widen can also mean to make something bigger in range. «Searching for new things on purpose widens what you see» means you see a bigger variety of things. Notice that the word is about size, but not always about a measurement you can touch.
explain: When eyes widen, they open more because of surprise or fear. «Her eyes widened» means she was surprised. Ask yourself: what would fit here? If you can swap in "opened more" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Widen means to make something wider, or to become wider.
fact: «The river widens near the sea» shows a river growing wider as it nears the sea.
fact: Widen can mean to increase the range of something, as in «widen your horizons».
fact: «Her eyes widened» means her eyes opened more because of surprise or fear.
fact: In maths and design, widening a shape changes its width and so changes its area.
exercise: «The river widens near the sea.» What does widens mean here? | Moves faster | *Gets wider | Gets shallower | Gets colder
exercise: «Her eyes widened in surprise.» What do widened eyes show? | They looked away | They closed tightly | *They opened more | They turned a different colour
exercise: Mia wants to widen the search for her lost cat. What does this mean? | Search only at night | *Look in more places | Stop looking | Search only one small room
test: Scientists say the Atlantic is still widening. What does widening mean here? | Drying up | Freezing over | Getting shallower | *Getting wider
test: Dad asks the council to widen the road so more cars can fit. What is the purpose? | *To make the road wider so more cars fit | To paint the road red | To make the road shorter | To close the road
exam: «Searching for new things on purpose widens what you see.» What does widens mean here? | Makes what you see darker | *Makes what you see bigger in range | Hides what you see | Makes what you see smaller
